WEBVTT

NOTE
Sample transcript for 8x-fathom-rebuild. Fictional company, fictional people.
Written to be awkward on purpose: crosstalk, a reversed decision, a number
nobody writes down, and one question the transcript deliberately never answers.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.400
<v Priya>Alright, we're recording. This is the Northwind renewal review — Dani, Marcus, Helen from their side, and Tom joining late.

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:16.200
<v Helen>Thanks Priya. I'll be direct: we're not signing a three-year this time. The board pushed back hard on the multi-year commitment.

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:19.100
<v Marcus>Pushed back on the term or on the—

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:25.900
<v Helen>On the term. The pricing is fine. It's the lock-in. We've had two vendors go sideways on us in eighteen months.

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:33.400
<v Priya>That's fair. So a one-year with the same rate, or a two-year with a break clause at twelve months?

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:40.800
<v Helen>The second one, if the break clause is genuinely unilateral. Not "with cause". We've been burned by "with cause".

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:48.300
<v Dani>I can't sign off on unilateral without Legal. I can tell you today that the rate holds either way, which I think is the bigger number.

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:55.700
<v Helen>It is the bigger number. What's the rate on the two-year, exactly? I don't want to be quoting the old one internally.

00:00:55.700 --> 00:01:02.100
<v Dani>I'll send it in writing rather than say it out loud and get it wrong. It's the same as your current effective rate.

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:09.600
<v Marcus>While we're here — the SSO migration. We said we'd do it before renewal. We have not done it before renewal.

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:15.200
<v Helen>No, and that's ours as much as yours. Our identity team went sideways in March.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:23.800
<v Marcus>Right. So do we make it a condition of the renewal, or do we decouple it and run it as its own project in Q1?

00:01:23.800 --> 00:01:29.400
<v Priya>Condition. If it isn't in the contract it doesn't happen, we both know that.

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:37.900
<v Dani>I'd push back on that. Making it a condition means the renewal can't close until Legal, Identity and our platform team all line up. That's not a December close.

00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:41.200
<v Priya>...Yes. Alright, I'm wrong. Decouple it.

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:49.700
<v Priya>Decision: two-year with a twelve-month break clause pending Legal, rate unchanged, SSO runs as a separate Q1 project with its own dates.

00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:56.300
<v Tom>Sorry — joining late. Did we land on whether SSO is blocking?

00:01:56.300 --> 00:02:01.800
<v Marcus>Not blocking. Separate project, Q1, dates to be set. You own the dates, Tom.

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:09.400
<v Tom>I can have a plan by the end of next week. I'll need someone from their identity team though, and in March that was the problem.

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:15.100
<v Helen>You'll have Ravi. He's back from leave on the eighth and this is his first thing.

00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:23.600
<v Dani>One risk I want on the record: if Legal comes back and won't do unilateral, we're back to a one-year and that changes the forecast.

00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:28.900
<v Priya>Noted. Dani, when do we hear from Legal?

00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:34.200
<v Dani>I'll have an answer by Thursday. If it's a no I'll flag it the same day rather than sit on it.

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:42.700
<v Helen>That works. Last thing from us — the reporting export. It still doesn't include the custom fields and we've asked three times.

00:02:42.700 --> 00:02:46.100
<v Marcus>Three times is three times too many. That's a bug, not a—

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:52.300
<v Marcus>—not a roadmap item. I'll get it into the next release and tell you the date rather than the quarter.

00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:58.800
<v Priya>Good. So: Legal by Thursday, SSO plan by end of next week, export fix with a date attached.

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:03.400
<v Helen>And the rate in writing. That's the one my board will ask about first.

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:07.900
<v Dani>In writing today. Before five.

00:03:07.900 --> 00:03:12.200
<v Priya>Thanks everyone. I'll send the notes round.
